 "labels": [
  {
   "language": "en",
   "status": "official",
   "text": "Section 55(d)(2)(A): the alternative minimum taxable income above which the joint-return / surviving-spouse exemption phases out. Statutory $150,000 (2012 base); section 55(d)(4)(A)(ii)(I) substitutes $1,000,000 for taxable years beginning after 2017 (as amended by Pub. L. 119-21 section 70107(a), which strikes the 2026 sunset, its (b) resetting the indexing base of this amount to 2025). 2025: Rev. Proc. 2024-40 section 2.11; 2026: Rev. Proc. 2025-32 section 4.10. Years between the anchored rows are NOT pinned in this package (no Revenue Procedure text for them is in us.irc.inflation_adjustments): evaluation returns MISSING_PARAMETER_VALUE there instead of a fabricated indexed figure (TECH-GAPS, income-individual stage 2 AMT)."
  }
 ],
